[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107657,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papilloma is a benign papillary tumour composed of M&uuml;llerian-type epithelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107658,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107659,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GA15.0 Polyp of cervix uteri</p>\r\n<p>GA14.0 Polyp of vagina</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107660,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> M&uuml;llerian papilloma of infancy.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> mesonephric papilloma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107661,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107662,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papillomas may arise in the cervix or vagina, and in some cases both sites may be involved {26948653}. The tumours are usually mucosal, but some vaginal examples are intramural. Their anatomical location in the cervix/vagina is variable {26948653}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107663,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with vaginal bleeding {26948653}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107664,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare cervical/vaginal neoplasms that mostly occur in prepubertal girls, typically aged 2&ndash;5&nbsp;years, with a few cases reported in adolescents or young adults (age range: 15&nbsp;months to 24&nbsp;years) {26948653; 17703455; 25330952; 21073126; 11737317; 9891250}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107665,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown, but it is likely to be developmental.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107666,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis of M&uuml;llerian papillomas is uncertain, but they are believed to arise from M&uuml;llerian epithelium {9891250; 6170416}. There have been reports of isolated cases with a history of another tumour/disorder, including renal cysts and Wilms tumour {15708065}, osteosarcoma {26948653}, and Proteus syndrome {23091906}, but there is insufficient evidence for a specific association. They are unrelated to either acquired or maternal HPV infection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107667,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucosal-based papillomas manifest as a friable polypoid lesion in the cervix and/or vagina {26948653; 17703455; 25330952}, whereas intramural tumours manifest as a solid-cystic mass in the vaginal wall {9891250; 6170416}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107668,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papillomas have a papillary architecture with branching fibrovascular stromal cores lined by cuboidal or columnar epithelium with no hobnail appearance or cytological atypia {17703455; 11737317; 9891250; 19616458}. Nuclei are bland with fine chromatin. Mitoses are normally absent. Squamous metaplasia may be seen. A rare case associated with melanin pigmentation has been reported {11737317}. There should be no stromal cell atypia or cambium layer; if present, these should raise the suspicion of rhabdomyosarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107669,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is little published information. The presence of glandular and papillary fragments with epithelial cells with hyperchromatic nuclei and a high N:C&nbsp;ratio was reported in 1&nbsp;case of cervical M&uuml;llerian papilloma {17703455}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107670,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107671,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> papillary architecture; cuboidal or columnar epithelium without cytological atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107672,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107673,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 277,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical outcome is favourable {26948653; 19616458}, although recurrence has been noted in a few cases {9526823; 30406704; 7979569; 10193336}. Malignant transformation to clear cell carcinoma was reported in 1&nbsp;case with multiple recurrences {12713630}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:19:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]